ands of Khamar-Daban Ridge (Fig. 64). Photos of localities along altitudinal gradient of Khamar-Daban Ridge are shown in Figures 65 – 71. Two species of the new genus Baikalozercon coexist on the same Khamar-Daban Ridge, but inhabit different altitudes — B. dracunculus occurs at altitudes of 500 – 700 m a. s. l. in mountain taiga and B. irbis at 1000 – 1600 m in alpine sparse forest with meadow and alpine tundra (Fig. 72).","","text","",""]]},"MLYW2":{"d":[["France","48144","mrgid","native",""]]},"MPC8C":{"d":[["humid ne Queensland between Endeavour and Burdekin rivers (ne Australia)","","text","",""]]},"MZMG":{"d":[["Australia (South Australia)","","text","",""]]},"N2PSX":{"d":[["Type locality Nii-jima Island, Izu Seven Islands Group, Tokyo Prefecture, Japan.","","text","",""]]},"N2Q2X":{"d":[["Distribution. China (Fujian).","","text","",""]]},"NFZCJ":{"d":[["Afrotropic","","text","native",""]]},"NHNW":{"d":[["Belgium","14","mrgid","",""],["Ireland","2114","mrgid","",""]]},"P7XLP":{"d":[["Distr.: Brazil – states of Rio de Janeiro and São Paulo; Guatemala, México, Nicarágua, Panamá.","","text","",""]]},"PK4Y3":{"d":[["Gulf of Mexico","4288","mrgid","native",""],["Gulf of Mexico","4288","mrgid","native",""]]},"PQVD":{"d":[["","CA","iso","",""],["","US","iso","",""]]},"PTGVZ":{"d":[["Distribution: Widely distributed in sub-Saharan Africa, but records scattered. In Madagascar, probably distributed all over the forested areas of the island, at middle altitude (250 – 730 m asl.).","","text","",""]]},"Q3H69":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"QWP8K":{"d":[["South America","","text","",""]]},"QXXDV":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"R25ZH":{"d":[["Distribution: Vietnam, China.","","text","",""]]},"RMM8W":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"RP3F":{"d":[["Vietnam","","text","",""]]},"RWDN":{"d":[["","BZL","tdwg","",""],["","BZS","tdwg","",""]]},"T7LTP":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"TBYXT":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]}